# REQUIRES: python-api, jax, torch, cuda
# mdir.jax against mdir.torch.evaluate on the same programs and frames
# (D371, D[frame-evaluator-jax-cuda]), on a CUDA device: programs of the
# GPU, and the arrays of JAX on the device, in the deterministic mode,
# double and mixed precision, Inputs/python_frames_jax.py: an interpreter with PyTorch
# writes the energies of three frames of the dipeptide and their gradients
# (in the positions, the edges of the cells, and the tunables, under a
# cotangent of weights) and those of water in a triclinic cell; the
# interpreter with JAX gives the same numbers, to the bit. The two adapters
# form the gradient in the cell with one function of the extension. XLA's
# deterministic ops are on: the sum over the frames of the VJP is a
# reduction of XLA on the device, whose order is otherwise chosen when it
# compiles (D[frame-evaluator-jax-cuda]).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide torch-dump Double GPU %t/double.npz | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DUMP -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: env XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false XLA_FLAGS=--xla_gpu_deterministic_ops=true %jax_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide torch-compare Double GPU %t/double.npz | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide torch-dump Mixed GPU %t/mixed.npz | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DUMP -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# RUN: env XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false XLA_FLAGS=--xla_gpu_deterministic_ops=true %jax_python %S/Inputs/python_frames_jax.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide torch-compare Mixed GPU %t/mixed.npz | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# DUMP: [[MODE]]: mdir.torch.evaluate written
# DUMP: torch passed
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: against mdir.torch.evaluate, the energies, to the bit: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: against mdir.torch.evaluate, the gradient in the positions, to the bit: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: against mdir.torch.evaluate, the gradient in the edges of the cells, to the bit: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: against mdir.torch.evaluate, the gradient in params under a cotangent of ones (the VJP), to the bit: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: against mdir.torch.evaluate, the energy in a triclinic cell, to the bit: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: against mdir.torch.evaluate, the gradient in its diagonal and its tilts, to the bit: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: against mdir.torch.evaluate, its gradient in params, to the bit: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: against mdir.torch.evaluate, the gradient in params under a cotangent of weights: largest relative difference
# CHECK: jax passed
